  "font_char_info_intro": "A font maps the cells of its texture to characters. Stelaris only allows characters of the Unicode Private Use Area for this. Unicode leaves these characters without meaning, so a custom glyph never replaces a letter, digit or emoji that players type or see in chat.",
  "font_char_info_areas_title": "Private Use Areas",
  "font_char_info_areas": "There are three areas: E000–F8FF with 6,400 characters, and the planes 15 (F0000–FFFFD) and 16 (100000–10FFFD) with about 65,000 characters each. Minecraft supports all three.",
  "font_char_info_input_title": "Input",
  "font_char_info_input": "The characters have no visible shape outside the game, so you type and see them as hex code points, separated by spaces: E000 E001 E002. A code point has 4 to 6 hex digits.",
