  "font_char_info_rows": "Each line stands for one row of the texture grid, from left to right, and the lines go from top to bottom. Minecraft cuts the texture into cells by the number of lines and their length, so all lines must have the same length. A texture with 3×2 icons needs 2 lines of 3 code points, a strip of 6 icons on top of each other needs 6 lines of 1 code point.",
